{"actor":{"id":"SUR","name":"Suriname","type":"state","iso2":"sr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suriname","coords":[-55.17,5.87],"seat":"Paramaribo","regions":["world"],"card":"full","tier":"minor","last_verified":"2026-10-16","dataset":"wikidata","grand_strategy":{"objectives":[{"rank":1,"text":"Turn the Block 58 offshore oil (GranMorgu) into state revenue once it starts, now expected by mid-2028. The investors are TotalEnergies and APA Corp, with Staatsolie, the state company, entitled to 20% under the production sharing contract. Our reading: the source gives the project and its timing, not a government statement of purpose, so the objective is inferred.","confidence":"C","sources":[{"url":"https://kvia.com/ap-national-news/2024/10/01/french-and-us-companies-to-invest-10-billion-to-extract-oil-off-surinames-coast/","title":"French and US companies to invest $10 billion to extract oil off Suriname's coast","publisher":"Associated Press (via KVIA)","date":"2024-10-01","tier":3}]},{"rank":2,"text":"Keep the Netherlands close, the one partner read so far with kinship under it. King Willem-Alexander and Queen Maxima made a state visit to Suriname on 1-3 December 2025, at President Geerlings-Simons' invitation.","confidence":"B","sources":[{"url":"https://www.royal-house.nl/latest/news/2025/10/10/state-visit-to-suriname","title":"State visit to Suriname","publisher":"Royal House of the Netherlands","date":"2025-10-10","tier":1}]}],"means":[{"text":"Oil as a lever. Staatsolie's 20% entitlement under the production sharing contract, in a project run by TotalEnergies and APA Corp with first oil expected by mid-2028 at about 220,000 barrels a day. One tier-3 wire report, so confidence C.","confidence":"C","sources":[{"url":"https://kvia.com/ap-national-news/2024/10/01/french-and-us-companies-to-invest-10-billion-to-extract-oil-off-surinames-coast/","title":"French and US companies to invest $10 billion to extract oil off Suriname's coast","publisher":"Associated Press (via KVIA)","date":"2024-10-01","tier":3}]},{"text":"A diplomatic channel to The Hague. The December 2025 state visit is the most visible tool, with the Royal House's own announcement as the source.","confidence":"B","sources":[{"url":"https://www.royal-house.nl/latest/news/2025/10/10/state-visit-to-suriname","title":"State visit to Suriname","publisher":"Royal House of the Netherlands","date":"2025-10-10","tier":1}]}],"constraints":[{"text":"Debt and the IMF. Suriname held about US$3.5 billion of debt and was in a three-year IMF restructuring programme when AP reported in October 2024. The oil money that would ease that load is not expected before mid-2028. The programme's status in 2026 was not read.","confidence":"C","sources":[{"url":"https://kvia.com/ap-national-news/2024/10/01/french-and-us-companies-to-invest-10-billion-to-extract-oil-off-surinames-coast/","title":"French and US companies to invest $10 billion to extract oil off Suriname's coast","publisher":"Associated Press (via KVIA)","date":"2024-10-01","tier":3}]}],"paradoxes":[{"text":"The oil that is meant to close the debt gap is run by foreign operators, with Staatsolie entitled to only 20%. The state's share of the early income therefore depends on contract terms the AP report does not give. Our reading, confidence C.","confidence":"C","sources":[{"url":"https://kvia.com/ap-national-news/2024/10/01/french-and-us-companies-to-invest-10-billion-to-extract-oil-off-surinames-coast/","title":"French and US companies to invest $10 billion to extract oil off Suriname's coast","publisher":"Associated Press (via KVIA)","date":"2024-10-01","tier":3}]}],"reading":"Suriname's strategy in 2026 is to bridge from a debt-and-IMF present to the 2028 oil start, with the Netherlands kept close as the partner that has kinship under it. The sources here are thin: one tier-3 wire report covers the oil, debt and IMF, and the Dutch card's tier-1 Royal House page covers the visit. China, Guyana, France, India and the United States have not been read from Paramaribo's side, so their postures are not yet written.\n"},"stale":false},"stances":[{"toward":"NLD","grade":"partner","trend":"warming","bond":"kin","since":"1975-11-25","last_verified":"2026-10-16","confidence":"C","reciprocal_of":"NLD","note":"Provisional mirror of the Dutch card's stance toward Suriname (NLD to SUR: partner, warming, bond kin), with the same sources and one grade lower. Nothing was read from Paramaribo's side, so this is C until written from the Surinamese side. Bond kin: shared language and history, and a large Surinamese diaspora in the Netherlands. The state visit of 1-3 December 2025, at President Geerlings-Simons' invitation, is the warm fact on this side too.","sources":[{"url":"https://www.royal-house.nl/latest/news/2025/10/10/state-visit-to-suriname","title":"State visit to Suriname","publisher":"Royal House of the Netherlands","date":"2025-10-10","tier":1},{"url":"https://ifacca.org/news/2026/01/13/directorate-culture-fund-discusses-strengthening-c/","title":"Directorate of the Culture Fund discusses strengthening cultural cooperation with Suriname","publisher":"IFACCA","date":"2026-01-13","tier":3}],"stale":false,"alignment":null}],"stances_toward":[{"toward":"SUR","grade":"partner","trend":"warming","bond":"kin","since":"1975-11-25","last_verified":"2026-10-12","confidence":"B","note":"The Dutch-speaking former colony with a large diaspora in the Netherlands: King Willem-Alexander and Queen Maxima made a state visit on 1-3 Dec 2025 at President Simons' invitation, the first by a reigning Dutch monarch since 1978, despite Simons' NDP having been founded by Bouterse, convicted in both countries. Dutch MPs asked in June 2025 for a diaspora policy so that other states do not fill the vacuum; cultural cooperation was agreed in January 2026. Warming. Bond - kin: language and history.","sources":[{"url":"https://www.royal-house.nl/latest/news/2025/10/10/state-visit-to-suriname","title":"State visit